@startuml
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam class {
  BorderColor #455A64
  ArrowColor #455A64
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #BDBDBD
}
title Architecture overview
caption Each package has one job. The web page only talks to the session; the grading model never depends on the web layer.

class web <<package>> #E8EAF6
class session <<package>> #E0F2F1
class progress <<package>> #F3E5F5
class submission <<package>> #E3F2FD
class tester <<package>> #E3F2FD
class execution <<package>> #FFF3E0
class scoring <<package>> #FFFDE7
class reporting <<package>> #E8F5E9
class style <<package>> #FCE4EC
class similarity <<package>> #EDE7F6
class feedback <<package>> #FFEBEE

web ..> session
web ..> progress

session ..> tester
session ..> submission
session ..> execution
session ..> reporting

execution ..> progress

reporting ..> scoring
reporting ..> style
reporting ..> similarity
reporting ..> feedback

note as Roles
  <b>What each package does</b> (all except web are in the grading package)
  web: the page and its HTTP routes (view and controller)
  session: one grading run at a time
  progress: live status shown on the page
  submission: validate and fix submissions
  tester: validate the tester folder
  execution: compile and run with time limits
  scoring: per-question and per-student marks
  reporting: PDF reports and the CSV score sheet
  style: CS102 style score
  similarity: plagiarism detection
  feedback: explains each mistake

  Arrows show the main dependencies only. Every package
  also reads grading.config (settings) and
  grading.assessment (the exam layout).
end note
@enduml
